This looks like October 2023. The fed funds rate is 5.33%, the 10-year yield is 4.59% after a sharp rise, and the 20y+ Treasuries fell 7.5% in one month. Headline CPI of 3.7% matches September 2023, and the 12-month equity returns also fit.

A check against the other candidate months: September 2023 had a 10-year yield of about 4.57% and CPI of 3.7% (August 3.7%, September 3.7%). Equity returns were -4.9% in September, against about -2.1% in October. Payrolls over three months averaged about 150k in September, which fits. The 10-year yield rose 0.78 over three months, from about 3.81% in June to 4.59% in September, which also fits. Treasuries 20y+ fell 7.5% in September, a better match than October. So the snapshot is September 2023.

